    "type": "question",
    "label": "2",
    "prompt": "The resultant vector is $\\binom{-2}{5}$ when adding vectors $\\binom{a}{3}$ and $\\binom{-5}{b}$. Find the values of $a$ and $b$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$a=3,\\ b=2$",
      "worked": "$$\\binom{a-5}{3+b}=\\binom{-2}{5}$$\nEquating corresponding components:\n$$\\begin{aligned}a-5&=-2\\\\a&=3\\end{aligned}\\qquad\\begin{aligned}3+b&=5\\\\b&=2\\end{aligned}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
